// RAMPAGE INDUCER (v18.99e): the BO6 aether canister — the device BO6 uses as
// its Rampage Inducer — from the MadGaz Liberty Falls pack (TOOLS-side
// bo6_props.gdt + model_export/_bo6, the same pack the perk machines come
// from; map 1 zones the _on twin as lab dressing, so it is proven to build).
// v14.20-v18.99d it was map 1's ww2_circuit_breaker power-switch model, which
// players read as a power switch and never as a rampage inducer. Both twins:
// _tod_rampage.gsc swaps to _on (lit purple gauge) while the mode is armed.
// v18.99h: the model is the REAL one now. It is
// `t10_zm_essence_container_orange` plus the four crystal shards
// `t10_zm_essence_container_crystal_01..04` that float in its glass
// cylinder, joined into ONE static prop (15 x 15 x 31 in, 7 materials) by
// tools/bo6_extraction/stage_rampage_inducer.py + install_inducer_bo3.py,
// which own source_data/tod_bo6_inducer.gdt and model_export/tod_bo6_inducer/.
//
// ITS ASSET NAME CONTAINS NEITHER "RAMPAGE" NOR "INDUCER" - both return 0 of
// 272,642 loaded BO6 assets and no public datamine names it. It was found by
// searching the FICTION (`kind:model essence`), because the wikis call it "an
// Aetherium essence canister containing fragments of a Fury Crystal".
// v18.99e-g shipped t10_zm_aether_canister, a Liberty Falls hazmat DRUM picked
// on a name match - measured, a constant-radius cylinder with a blue-violet
// gauge glow and no crystal in it at all.
// docs/208: THE CYBER INDUCER replaces the canister above - map 1's own device
// (its 2026-10-02 v19.68m, ported whole): plinth + RAMPAGE display, copper coil,
// four ribs caging a levitating Fury crystal cluster in a plasma column, finned
// crown with claws and a beacon. ONE model, five animated bones
// (source_data/tod_inducer_cyber.gdt, model_export/ + xanim_export/tod_inducer_cyber/,
// held to art/rampage_inducer_cyber/install_manifest.json by tools/inducer_cyber/verify.py).
// The canister's GDT and model files stay on disk UNZONED as the rollback - put
// `xmodel,tod_inducer` + `xmodel,tod_inducer_on` back here and point
// _tod_rampage.gsc's TOD_RAMPAGE_MODEL* at them (and drop its anim_set call).
xmodel,tod_inducer_cyber
// The LIT twin - same xmodel_bin, skinOverride to the `_on` materials (rampage
// red trims, the hot ON glow map). Script swaps to it while rampage is on.
xmodel,tod_inducer_cyber_on
// ITS MOTION - two looping clips (idle 12 s / on 3 s) on those bones, and the
// animtree _tod_rampage.gsc's #using_animtree names. All three lines are
// required: an xanim missing from the zone plays nothing and says nothing.
rawfile,animtrees/tod_inducer.atr
xanim,tod_inducer_cyber_loop_idle
xanim,tod_inducer_cyber_loop_on
// ITS GLOW (v18.99i, user: "it needs to glow a dim orange of some sort. And
// then when it's on, it needs to pulse a deeper orange ... when it's off, it
// just has, like, a dim kinda lamp"). Two looping effects off one donor -
// map 1's amber perk aura - written by tools/gen_tod_inducer_fx.py. Each keeps
// the donor's real dynamic light; idle is flat at 200, on pulses 300-900 once a
// second in a deeper orange. WITHOUT THESE TWO LINES the effects silently never
// play and the device just sits there dark.
fx,tod/fx_tod_inducer_idle
fx,tod/fx_tod_inducer_on
